  "script": "I've sailed through the Bermuda Triangle thirty-one times. Here's my report. Weather. The Gulf Stream is fast, storms build quickly, and it's one of the busiest stretches of ocean on Earth. More boats means more accidents. Studies have found no more ships go missing there than anywhere else that busy. The name itself came from a magazine story in 1964. The Triangle isn't swallowing ships. It's selling books."
